From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] touch: nt383x0: report tap-to-wake as a power key on sol

Tapping sol's screen while it is off does not wake it. The touch firmware
reports its tap-to-wake gesture, and the driver turns it into one synthetic
finger tap. That is what Wear OS wants, but AsteroidOS's mce wakes the
display on a double tap: it recognises one from two real taps, or from a
power key released by the touchscreen. A single synthetic tap is neither.

Report the gesture as KEY_POWER, as the driver already does for its other
wake gestures. mce treats that as a double tap and applies its usual
doubletap policy. The module parameter sol_tap_wake_as_power (default 1)
restores the synthetic tap at runtime.

Untested on hardware: needs someone tapping the watch.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AsteroidOS sol: mce wakes on a double tap, Wear OS on a single tap]
---
diff --git a/private/google-modules/touch/novatek/nt383x0/nt383x0.c b/private/google-modules/touch/novatek/nt383x0/nt383x0.c
--- a/private/google-modules/touch/novatek/nt383x0/nt383x0.c
+++ b/private/google-modules/touch/novatek/nt383x0/nt383x0.c
@@ -630,6 +630,16 @@
 return:
 	Executive outcomes. 0---succeed. negative---failed.
 *******************************************************/
+/*
+ * AsteroidOS's mce wakes the display on a double tap, which it recognises
+ * either from two real taps or from a power key released by the touchscreen.
+ * The firmware's tap-to-wake gesture arrives as one synthetic tap, which mce
+ * never pairs into a double tap. Report it as KEY_POWER instead, like the
+ * other wake gestures here; 0 restores the synthetic tap.
+ */
+static bool sol_tap_wake_as_power = true;
+module_param(sol_tap_wake_as_power, bool, 0644);
+
 int nvt_ts_wakeup_gesture_report(uint8_t gesture_id, uint8_t *data)
 {
 	uint32_t keycode = 0;
@@ -658,6 +668,12 @@
 				break;
 			}
 
+			if (sol_tap_wake_as_power) {
+				NVT_LOG("Gesture : Tap to Wake, reported as KEY_POWER\n");
+				keycode = KEY_POWER;
+				break;
+			}
+
 			NVT_LOG("Gesture : Tap to Wake, coordinates (%d,%d) instead of keycode.\n",
 				input_x, input_y);
 			/* Send finger down */
